# Code owners for the MCP parity gate and the workflows that enforce it.
#
# The parity test decides which web endpoints may stay out of the MCP.
# Weakening it (an exclusion, the verifier, the behavioural bearer test,
# the guard) lets an API-key-callable endpoint skip the MCP. Changes need a
# code-owner review, and parity-exclusion-guard additionally requires the
# code owner's approving review on the current head plus the
# `parity-exclusion-approved` label applied by the code owner
# (.github/workflows/parity-exclusion-guard.yml).
#
# All workflows are owned: a PR could otherwise add a look-alike workflow
# whose job reports the same check name as the guard.
#
# The test-runner wiring of the MCP is owned too: dropping or filtering the
# parity test from the run would bypass it without touching the test.
#
# parity-endpoint-tools.json is deliberately not owned: every mapping in it
# is proven by the parity test, so adding an MCP tool needs no approval.

